\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The Room Without Corners\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 You step into the room because the door was already open.\uc0\u8232 You do not remember walking here, but the faint ache in your legs suggests the journey was not short.\u8232 The air is still, holding the sort of hush that feels borrowed from a library where all the books are asleep.\u8232 And it is not a square room.\
At first, you think it is round, but then your eyes adjust and you see that the walls bend away in ways that refuse geometry.\uc0\u8232 No corners.\u8232 No edges.\u8232 Only smooth curves that seem to lean away from you when you look too closely.\
In the center: a table, its wood dark as wet soil.\uc0\u8232 On the table: a single envelope, unsealed, face down.\u8232 No handwriting, only an embossed mark \'97 a circle with a single, hairline crack running through it.\
You are tempted to turn it over, but there is a voice \'97 perhaps yours \'97 that whispers:\
If you touch it, the arrangement changes.\
The arrangement of what?\uc0\u8232 No answer comes.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 The Corridor That Wasn\'92t There Before\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 You remember the room having only one door \'97 the one you entered through \'97 but now there is a second opening, tall and thin like an exclamation mark carved in shadow.\
The corridor is narrow. The floor is stone, damp in some places, warm in others. You hear nothing but the faint scrape of your own steps.\uc0\u8232 The walls seem to swell and contract, subtly, as though breathing.\
Halfway down, you see a small recess in the wall: a shelf, barely large enough for the object that rests on it.\uc0\u8232 It is a watch.\u8232 The face is black. The hands are white.\u8232 They are moving \'97 but not forward.\u8232 The second hand ticks once, then disappears for two beats, then returns, pointing somewhere unexpected.\
When you lean closer, you realize the numbers on the watch are not numbers at all. They are words:\uc0\u8232 
\f0\b \'93If,\'94 \'93You,\'94 \'93Read,\'94 \'93This,\'94 \'93Then,\'94 \'93It\'92s,\'94 \'93Too,\'94 \'93Late.\'94
\f1\b0 \
You look away quickly, but the rhythm of the ticking follows you like a sentence you haven\'92t finished reading.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 The Voice in the Hall of Mirrors\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The corridor bends without warning, spilling you into a hall lined with mirrors.\uc0\u8232 The frames are mismatched: some gilded, some cracked, some with no frame at all.\u8232 They all reflect you, and they all disagree on what \'93you\'94 is.\
In one, you are wearing a coat you\'92ve never owned.\uc0\u8232 In another, your face is turned away from the glass, though you stand directly before it.\u8232 One mirror shows the room you started in \'97 empty, except for the envelope, now upright and open.\
Somewhere among the reflections, a voice speaks:\
\'93You\'92ve already been here twice.\'94\
The statement is impossible, but it lands with the weight of memory.\uc0\u8232 You try to speak, to ask what it means, but the mirrors show your mouth moving and no sound leaving.\u8232 Only in one reflection do you see your breath fog the glass.\u8232 Only in one does the fog spell out words before fading:\
\'93You\'92re not asking the right question.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 The Stairs That Lead Sideways\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 You choose one mirror at random and press your hand to the glass.\uc0\u8232 It is cold but gives way, folding like fabric.\u8232 You fall through, but instead of down, you fall sideways.\
You land on a staircase.\uc0\u8232 It climbs and descends at the same time \'97 the steps tilt, so each footfall is both upward and downward.\u8232 At the top, there is another top. At the bottom, there is another bottom.\u8232 And halfway, there is a door in the wall, just large enough to crouch through.\
When you open it, you find yourself staring into an empty picture frame nailed to a wall of black stone.\uc0\u8232 Behind the frame is not stone at all, but a slow-moving fog.\u8232 It coils, rearranges, then seems to form a sentence before unraveling:\u8232 
\f0\b \'93This is where you left the answer.\'94
\f1\b0 \
You step closer.\uc0\u8232 The fog rushes forward.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 The Library of Missing Pages\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 It swallows you whole and deposits you \'97 gently \'97 into a library.\uc0\u8232 The shelves are high, higher than the ceiling should allow.\u8232 Ladders stretch up endlessly, their tops lost in shadows.\
Every book is missing something.\uc0\u8232 Some lack titles, others lack covers, others are just frames of paper with holes where the text should be.\u8232 A book sits open on the nearest desk, its left page blank, its right page containing only three words:\
\'93Look behind you.\'94\
You turn, but the library remains empty.\uc0\u8232 Then you notice that the desk is no longer a desk, but a coffin-shaped box.\u8232 Inside is not a body, but a scattering of envelopes, each marked with that same broken circle.\u8232 All are sealed.\
You choose one.\uc0\u8232 It is warm to the touch.\u8232 It thrums faintly, like a heartbeat you can\'92t decide is yours.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 The Return to the Room Without Corners\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 You blink, and the library is gone.\uc0\u8232 You are back in the first room.\u8232 The table is still there, still dark, still damp-looking.\
The envelope is now open.\uc0\u8232 Inside, there is nothing \'97 no letter, no photograph, no key.\u8232 Only the faintest trace of a smell: rain on iron.\
The voice returns, softer now:\
\'93It isn\'92t here anymore.\'94\
You ask what \'93it\'94 is.\uc0\u8232 The voice says nothing.\u8232 The walls curve further away, as though trying to avoid you.\
You realize, then, that the door you first entered through is gone.\uc0\u8232 The second door \'97 the one to the corridor \'97 is gone as well.\
The room without corners is now a room without exits.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 The Clock Without Hands\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 When the table disappears, it does so without ceremony.\uc0\u8232 In its place is the watch you saw before.\u8232 It has no hands now \'97 only the black face, and the faint impression where the words used to be.\
You can\'92t read them anymore, but you can hear them, faint and deliberate, as though spoken from just inside your own head:\
\'93If you read this, then it\'92s too late.\'94\
And then, after a pause that feels longer than it should be:\
\'93But it always was.\'94
\f0\b\fs36 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The Corridor That Breathes\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The watch fades, not with a blink, but with a slow thinning of presence \'97 like watching fog dissolve under a patient wind.\uc0\u8232 In its place, a corridor forms.\u8232 It is the same length as the one you walked earlier, but you know it is not the same corridor.\
The air moves here, but not from any breeze.\uc0\u8232 It moves in time with a pulse you cannot locate.\u8232 With every step, the walls expand slightly, then contract.\u8232 The sound is not breathing exactly, but it is close enough that your body reacts as if it were \'97 your own chest trying to keep pace.\
Halfway through, you notice patterns in the wall.\uc0\u8232 At first they seem like cracks, then like letters, then like something older than both \'97 shapes meant to be read by a mind that does not live in your skull.\
One shape in particular draws you in: a spiral, but with no center.\uc0\u8232 You trace it with your finger, and for a heartbeat you feel a presence behind the wall, tracing you back.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 The Well With No Depth\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The corridor ends in a circular chamber.\uc0\u8232 At its center: a well.\u8232 The stones are worn smooth, as though countless hands have leaned over its edge.\
You approach and look down.\uc0\u8232 There is no reflection, no ripple, no water \'97 just darkness.\u8232 Yet when you lean closer, you hear dripping, slow and irregular.\
You drop a small piece of loose stone into the well.\uc0\u8232 It does not clink against walls, does not splash.\u8232 It falls without sound, without end.\
A voice rises from below, muffled as if through heavy cloth:\
\'93You put it in the wrong one.\'94\
You step back, heart unsteady.\uc0\u8232 The dripping stops.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 The Door That Refuses to Open\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 On the far side of the chamber is a wooden door, blackened with age.\uc0\u8232 You press your hand to it \'97 the wood is warm, faintly vibrating.\
The handle turns easily, but the door does not open.\uc0\u8232 You push harder.\u8232 It still does not open.\
Then you realize: the hinge side keeps switching.\uc0\u8232 Every time you blink, the door\'92s orientation changes \'97 now it should swing left, now right, now inward, now outward \'97 but it never does.\
As you stand there, it occurs to you that perhaps the door has no other side.\uc0\u8232 It exists only here, for you to fail at opening it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 The Room of Quiet Hands\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 When you give up on the door, you find yourself elsewhere.\uc0\u8232 It is not a transition \'97 there is no fading, no shift \'97 simply, the door is gone and the space around you is new.\
This room is filled with hands.\uc0\u8232 They emerge from the walls, the ceiling, the floor \'97 pale, still, perfectly clean.\u8232 Some are open, some are closed into fists, some point toward things you cannot see.\
You step carefully between them, avoiding their reach.\uc0\u8232 At first they do not move.\u8232 Then one \'97 just one \'97 brushes the back of your neck with a fingertip colder than stone.\
The voice returns, but now it comes from multiple directions at once, as though the hands themselves are speaking:\
\'93It\'92s not the object. It\'92s the order.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 The Order That Doesn\'92t Matter\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The phrase follows you into the next hall.\uc0\u8232 It repeats itself in different tones, different voices, until the meaning collapses under the weight of repetition.\
You start thinking of every step you\'92ve taken since arriving.\uc0\u8232 The room without corners.\u8232 The corridor.\u8232 The mirrors.\u8232 The stairs.\u8232 The library.\u8232 The watch.\u8232 The breathing corridor.\u8232 The well.\u8232 The door.\u8232 The hands.\
Was there an order?\uc0\u8232 If so, did you choose it?\u8232 Or did it choose you?\
You realize the sequence could be reversed and nothing would change.\uc0\u8232 The objects would still be meaningless.\u8232 The phrases would still be incomplete.\
You walk on, but with the strange feeling that you have been walking backward all along.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 The Window That Looks In\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 You arrive at a wall with a single window.\uc0\u8232 Through it, you see a room you do not recognize \'97 small, dim, with the faint outline of a table.\
On the table is an envelope.\uc0\u8232 It is sealed.\u8232 The mark on it is the broken circle.\
You look closer.\uc0\u8232 A figure enters the room \'97 someone with your height, your build, your posture.\u8232 They approach the envelope and hesitate.\
And then you understand: the window is not showing a room beyond the wall.\uc0\u8232 It is showing you, now, from somewhere else.\
The figure turns toward the window.\uc0\u8232 Its eyes are yours.\u8232 Its lips move, and though you cannot hear, you know the words:\
\'93If you touch it, the arrangement changes.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 The Room Without You\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 When you turn from the window, you are in the room without corners again.\uc0\u8232 The envelope is gone.\u8232 The table is gone.\u8232 Even the shadows seem less certain.\
You glance around for the doors.\uc0\u8232 There are none.\u8232 There is nothing here but the faint smell of rain on iron and the memory of something you were supposed to do but never did.\
The voice comes one last time \'97 or perhaps it has been speaking this whole time, and you only now realize it:\
\'93It was never a puzzle. You just wanted it to be.\'94\
The room leans away from you.\uc0\u8232 Or maybe you are leaning away from it.\u8232 And then there is only the space between breaths, stretched long enough to feel infinite.}